# Roobytes vim (not vanilla)

## Ergonomics & convention (required)

Roobytes is **Roobytes-flavored**, not a full Vim port — but Normal-mode bindings must still **respect Vim ergonomics and convention**:

1. **Prefer the canonical vim key** when the action matches a known verb (`K` = keyword/`keywordprg` lookup, `gx` = open URL under cursor, `u` = undo, `zz` = center, …).
2. **Home-row / shift pairs** stay familiar: lowercase motion (`k` up) vs uppercase command (`K` lookup); `g`/`G`, `o`/`O`, `p`/`P` follow the same case split.
3. **Do not invent cute chords** that steal or contradict muscle memory (`gd` ≠ Dictionary; `gk` is display-line up in vim — avoid for Look Up).
4. Roobytes-only ideas (tasks `md`/`mf`, folds `za`) may use free letters, but document them in `:h` and keep them consistent once shipped.
5. When choosing a new binding, ask: *Would a vim user guess this on the first try?* If not, prefer the vim analogue or a clear pending chord (`g…`) over a random single key.

## File map

- `EditorViewController+Vim.swift` — key dispatch, Esc, mode switch (Normal / Insert / Visual), insert placement
- `+VimMotions.swift` — h/j/k/l, w/b/e, scrolls, caret; Visual extends selection via `visualAnchor` / `visualCaret`
- `+VimEdits.swift` — dd/yy/put, tasks, folds, URL open, Look Up (`K`), spell fix (`z=`), undo
- `+VimCommandLine.swift` — `:`, help, tips, chord HUD, palette
- `+WordCompletion.swift` — Insert menu / ghost / accept
- `RoobytesEditorTextView.swift` — keyDown / insertText / doCommand gates · `VimVisual` selection math

## Vertical motion (`j` / `k`)

- **Bare `j`/`k` walk display rows** (wrapped paragraphs are reachable); **a count keeps logical lines** — `LineNumberGutterView` draws one hybrid relative number per logical line and labels the colors `j` / `k`, so `5j` must land on the row labelled `5`. Policy lives in `VimVerticalMotion.usesDisplayRows`; `gj`/`gk` force rows.
- Display rows walk `NSLayoutManager` line fragments. The trailing empty line after a final newline owns **no glyphs** (`extraLineFragment`) — **do not** land Normal-mode `j` / caret there (clamp via `caretLocationClampedOffTrailingEmpty`; `LineIndexCache` omits the phantom start at `length`). Insert may still edit that paragraph after `o`.
- Both paths keep a **sticky goal** (`vimVerticalGoalX` / `vimVerticalGoalColumn`) so passing a short line does not truncate the column. It is validated by `vimVerticalGoalAnchor` (the caret location the last vertical motion produced), so any other motion or edit drops it automatically — do not add manual invalidation to each motion.

## Caret (do not reintroduce blink)

- **Normal / Visual are steady; only Insert blinks.** `RoobytesEditorTextView.updateInsertionPointStateAndRestartTimer` forces `false` outside Insert.
- **Color role:** all “you are here” feedback uses `RoobytesAccent.caret` (the preset’s supplementary/bright companion): Normal block selection, Insert caret, pending underscore, checkbox ring, jump feedback, and titlebar mode dot. Task fills, focus wash, and pins stay on primary `RoobytesAccent.color`.
- Over a character the Normal caret is **not** an insertion point — it is a one-character selection (`refreshBlockCaret` + `RoobytesAccent.selectionAttributes`) so wide/CJK glyphs and checkbox attachments get exact width and a white glyph. Selections never blink.
- `drawInsertionPoint` only paints the block/underscore at EOL, blank lines, and EOF (selection length 0). Gate it on `flag || shouldDrawInsertionPoint` so an unfocused view still erases.
- **Task checkbox** — never select or fill it: `taskDoneFill` / `[!]` use the same accent as the selection paint, so a block there reads as one flat slab. `refreshBlockCaret` collapses on an `.attachment`, and `drawInsertionPoint` strokes a rounded ring around `checkboxSquareRect` (baseline-derived, excludes `checkboxTrailingGap`).

## Visual (thin characterwise)

- **`v`** — enter characterwise Visual from Normal (toggle `v` / Esc leave)
- Motions (`h/j/k/l`, `w/b/e`, `0/$`, `gg`/`G`, arrows, counts) extend an AppKit selection
- **`y`** — characterwise yank of the selection (markdown source via caret mapping); leave Visual at selection start **without** full Live Preview restyle
- **`d`** / **`x`** — characterwise cut (yank + delete); leave Visual at deletion start (restyles; same cost class as `dd`)
- Visual ops skip full attributed→markdown serialize when `activeSourceLine` is nil (normal Visual); map endpoints after any sync
- Format with **⌘B** / **⌘I** (no vim bold/italic operators)
- A persistent frosted `VISUAL · y yank · d cut · ⌘B/⌘I · Esc` badge sits bottom-left; keep bottom-right free for chord hints
- No linewise `V`, blockwise, or operator-pending motions on the range (yet)

## Yank / put

- **`yy`** — content yank: strip list/task markers and a leading `tag: ` (letters, digits, hyphens; e.g. `t:`, `wh-os:`, `2518:`). Fills pasteboard + `vimYankLines` (linewise).
- **`dd`** — full source line cut (markers included, linewise).
- Visual **`y`** / **`d`** fill the same register as **characterwise**; `p`/`P` insert after/before the caret character.
- **`yyp`** pastes body-only lines by design — not a bug.

## Tasks

- **`mf`** / **`'f`** — focus pin (`[!]` toggle / jump); one named destination
- **`]t`** / **`[t`** — next / previous undone task (`[ ]` or `[!]`); counts (`3]t`); no wrap, beep if none
- **`md`** / **`mD`** — mark done / open
- **Cascade:** open (or newly created) nested task reopens a done parent; all direct children done/deprecated completes the parent. Same rule on Enter / `o` / Esc after Insert.

## Links

- **`gx`** — open URL under caret in the **default browser** (`BrowserLauncher` / `NSWorkspace`)
- **`gX`** — Firefox Private when Firefox is installed; otherwise falls back to default browser

## Look Up

- **`K`** — system Dictionary / Look Up for the word under the caret (`WordUnderCaret` + `NSView.showDefinition`). Beep if none.
- **Why `K`:** classic vim runs `keywordprg` on the word under the cursor with **`K`** (often `man`). macOS Dictionary is the natural Roobytes stand-in. Free key (`k` remains up); Shift+`k` is one-handed and matches the motion/command case split.

## Spelling

- **`z=`** — auto-apply the **first** macOS `NSSpellChecker` guess for the word under the caret (markdown line). Flash `Fixed → …`; beep + `No suggestions` if none. No suggestion menu (Roobytes shortcut vs full vim `z=` picker).

## `:h` / VimHelp (required)

When adding or changing any Normal-mode binding (single key or chord), **always** update `VimHelp.swift` so `:h` / `:help` stays the source of truth. Also extend the `VimHelp.text.contains(…)` checks in `Tests/RoobytesCoreTests`. Do not leave help stale.

## Esc / control keys

- Esc with word-completion visible → dismiss menu **and** go to Normal (one press)
- Block Insert-mode control newlines: **`^O`**, **`^J`**, **`^M`** (must not leak as raw `\n` via `insertText`)
- Bare `\n`/`\r` in `insertText` must route through `insertNewlineContinuingList`

## New two-key chords

- Pending first key via `setPendingVimKey`; keep `vimCount` for motions like `dd`
- Add a `VimChordHints` entry for that pending key
- Land jumps on `contentStartColumn` and center when matching `'f` / `]t`

## Overlays

- File Switcher (`⌘P`), `:`, help/tips: claim first responder after menu actions (async refocus if needed)
- Do not leave Normal vim as first responder — it swallows typing while arrows may still work via monitors
- **`:h` scroll:** while help is open, **`⌃e`/`⌃y`** line and **`⌃d`/`⌃u`** half-page scroll the help panel (same chords as Normal viewport scroll). Esc / `q` dismiss.

## Word completion anchors

- Menu/ghost X/Y from **layout-manager glyph bounds** in text-view space, converted to the host view
- Never `firstRect` → screen → window; bogus X gets clamped to the trailing edge
